    {
      "id": "e55bc1df-2d9e-4159-ac1e-85f76cf90d2d",
      "name": "Sticky Note6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -160,
        -32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 768,
        "height": 992,
        "content": "## How it works\n\nThis workflow automatically converts a YouTube video into multiple types of social media content using AI.\n\nThe workflow starts when a YouTube video URL is received through a webhook. It extracts the video ID, fetches video details from YouTube, and collects the video transcript using Apify.\n\nThe transcript is cleaned and sent to OpenAI, which generates:\n\nLinkedIn post\nTwitter/X thread\nBlog content\nYouTube description\n\nThe workflow also creates a professional AI thumbnail prompt and generates a custom thumbnail image using OpenAI image generation.\n\nThe thumbnail image is uploaded to Google Drive, made publicly accessible, and its public link is stored.\n\nFinally, all generated content, transcript data, video details, and thumbnail URL are saved into a Notion database for easy content management and reuse.\n\n\n\n## Setup steps\n\n**1.** Create credentials for:\nYouTube API, OpenAI API, Apify API, Google Drive, Notion\n\n**2.** Connect all credentials inside n8n.\n**3.** Create a Notion database with fields for:\nVideo Title, Video URL, Transcript, inkedIn Post, Twitter Thread, Blog, YouTube, Description, Thumbnail URL, Timestamp\n**3.** Update the Notion Database ID in the workflow.\n**4.** Activate the workflow.\n**5.** Send a YouTube video URL to the webhook endpoint to generate AI content automatically."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
